--TEST--
a constructor's parameter is refused, because `new` can pass it by name and the index holds no `new` call as a call of the constructor, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Greeter
{
    private string $greeting;

    public function constructor(string $word)
    {
        $this->greeting = $wo<|>rd;
    }
}

echo new Greeter(word: "Hello")->greeting;
--REQUEST--
rename to=text
--EXPECT--
refused: `$word` is a parameter of a constructor, and `new` can pass it by name. It cannot be renamed.
